  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DEC funded emergency assistance to Ukrainian refugees arriving in Romania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partner: JRS Europe

Funding source: DEC appeal

Total number of direct beneficiaries (individuals): 1,048

Context: Both the Romanian authorities and civil society have recognised that the package of assistance offered by Romania under the European Union&#x2019;s Temporary Protection Mechanism (TPM)  is not sufficient, and does not allow a dignified and safe existence for refugees in Romania given the heightened risks for vulnerable women and children which exist across Eastern Europe.

Key activities: providing shelter, living allowance, communications and legal advice to Ukrainians arriving in Romania.

Activity split:
10%: Education in emergencies
20%: Food, nutrition &amp; livelihoods in emergencies
10%: Health in emergencies
10%: Non-food items in emergencies
10%: Protection in emergencies
40%: Shelter in emergencies</narrative>
  </description>
